    <briefdescription>
<para>Configurable anomaly detector that delegates to <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_z_score_detector" kindref="compound">ZScoreDetector</ref>, <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_i_q_r_detector" kindref="compound">IQRDetector</ref>, or both. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>When <ref refid="namespacethemis_1ac6ac6b1da215b6285e2111a58888ea36a130c5b3473c57faa76e2a1c54e26f88e" kindref="member">AnomalyMethod::Both</ref> is selected, the union of anomalies detected by either method is returned; duplicate timestamps are de-duplicated, keeping the entry with the higher absolute score.</para>
<para><heading level="3">Example</heading>
</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">AnomalyConfig<sp/>cfg;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cfg.method<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacethemis_1ac6ac6b1da215b6285e2111a58888ea36a0864acd24c328bdc0b2c2e8aa9ee4e03" kindref="member">AnomalyMethod::ZScore</ref>;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cfg.zscore_threshold<sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/>3.0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1_anomaly_detector_1a52789cf1f256ed1851dd026da5061a8c" kindref="member">AnomalyDetector</ref><sp/>detector(cfg);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>anomalies<sp/>=<sp/>detector.detect(points);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
